<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Günther von Schwarzburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1304–1349</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Günther XXI of Schwarzburg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Günther XXI of Schwarzburg was a Thuringian count elected King of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> in January 1349 by the Wittelsbach party as a rival to Charles IV. Lacking support and seriously ill, he renounced his claim in May 1349 in exchange for money and died weeks later in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt">Frankfurt</a>, where he was buried in the cathedral.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gunther-von-schwarzburg.jpg" alt="Günther von Schwarzburg" width="320" height="769" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Guenther_von_schwarzburg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
